<title>JAPAN: Mitsui Engineering wins Thai desulphuriser order.</title>
<headline>Mitsui Engineering wins Thai desulphuriser order.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsui Engineering &amp; Shipbuilding Co Ltd said on Tuesday it had won a turnkey contract from Thailand's Bangchak Petroleum Plc to build a 25,000 barrel-per-day deep gas oil desulphurising unit.</p>
<p>The 4.5 billion yen project will be completed by November 1998, Mitsui Engineering said in a statement.</p>
<p>Thai environmental regulations require all oil refineries to have deep gas oil desulphurisers from 1999, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Energy Desk +81-3-5473-3708</p>
</text>
